# Override ~/.gitignore_global's blanket ".claude/" rule for this repo.
#
# modules/dotfiles/macos/.claude/ is tracked dotfile *source*, deployed to
# ~/.claude/ via home-manager -- not a per-project Claude Code runtime
# directory. Without this override, any new file added under that tree is
# silently swallowed by `git add -A` / `git commit -a`: it won't even show
# up in `git status` (only `git status --ignored` reveals it), while
# modules/home.nix (already tracked) keeps referencing the missing file --
# breaking `darwin-rebuild switch` / `home-manager switch` on every other
# machine with "Path '...' does not exist in Git repository".
!modules/dotfiles/macos/.claude/
!modules/dotfiles/macos/.claude/**
